# OpenAPI Type Generation

## Generated files — never edit manually

Files in `src/types/generated/` are auto-generated from the OpenAPI specs at
`../admin/api/v2/{data,stats,ui,system}/definition.yaml` (paths relative to this package when it lives beside `admin/` in the self-hosted repo) by the script
`scripts/generate-types.mjs`. **Do not edit them by hand.**

## When to regenerate

Run the generator after **any** change to a `definition.yaml`:

```bash
pnpm generate-types
```

## Wrapper files

The parent files `entities.ts`, `api.ts`, `stats.ts`, `ui.ts` re-export
generated types and add hand-written extras (helper functions, app-only
types, type overrides). Place new hand-written types there, not in
`generated/`.

## Adding a new definition to YAML

1. Add the definition to the relevant `definition.yaml`
2. Run `pnpm generate-types` from this package root
3. Add a re-export to the appropriate wrapper file (`entities.ts`, `stats.ts`, etc.)
4. Import from the wrapper file in application code — never from `generated/` directly

## Script conventions

- `integer/int64` → `string` (all entity IDs are strings in the app)
- `integer/int32` → `number`
- `number/double` → `number`
- Enum lists > 30 values → `string` (avoids overly strict unions)
- `default: null` on strings → `string | null`
- Property rename: `idTrafficSouce` → `idTrafficSource` (spec typo)
- Definition renames: `Date` → `ApiDate`, `TimeHHMM` → `ApiTime`,
  `DateTime` → `ApiDateTime`, `DateTimeRange` → `ApiDateTimeRange`,
  `TimeZone` → `ApiTimeZone`, `Error` → `ApiErrorResponse`
